cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
title: "pywinratio: win ratio, net benefit and win odds for hierarchical composite outcomes in Python"
abstract: >-
  pywinratio computes the win ratio, the net benefit and the win odds for
  hierarchical composite outcomes. Patients are compared pair by pair on
  outcomes ranked by importance, which can be binary, ordinal, continuous or
  censored times to an event. The comparison can use every pair of patients,
  pairs within strata, matched pairs or weighted pairs, and handles patients
  clustered in hospitals. Confidence intervals come from U-statistic theory,
  the bootstrap or permutation tests. The package also does propensity-score
  matching and weighting, sensitivity analyses and sample-size calculations.
  Its results agree with the R packages BuyseTest and WINS.
